  "notes": "Sample pack for the tfmask Terraform secret-scanning CLI. sample.tfstate / clean.tfstate are valid Terraform state v4 (version 4, terraform_version 1.9.8, serial, lineage UUID, outputs, resources[]). sensitive_attributes entries use the real 'attributes.<name>' path form. clean.tfstate is the zero-false-positive control: no AKIA keys, no 40-char secret shapes, no credential-bearing DSNs, no PEM, no tokens - but it DOES retain an ssh-ed25519 public key and an ssh-rsa public key (vault data.public_key / data.ssh_keys) as intentional negative controls, since public keys are not secrets and a correct scanner must not flag them. All credential values are FAKE placeholders (AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE / wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY are the well-known AWS docs example pair; sk-proj-, ghp_, github_pat_, tok_live_, jwt and PEM bodies are synthetically shaped). plan-output.txt line numbers are 1-indexed and verified against the file. entropy_approx is Shannon entropy in bits/char over the decoded value (user_data entries are base64-decoded first)."
